WEBVTT

00:02.470 --> 00:05.440
In matters relating
to the world of the dead

00:05.540 --> 00:08.900
there is an institution that judges
the sins of the deceased

00:09.160 --> 00:10.700
the Ju-Oh-Cho.

00:11.540 --> 00:13.310
The Summons Section
of the Judgment Bureau

00:13.410 --> 00:17.140
comprises a group supporting
the ministry's operating functions

00:17.250 --> 00:20.080
by guiding the lost souls
that wander the mortal world.

00:20.450 --> 00:22.080
They are also known as...

00:22.320 --> 00:24.760
the Shinigami.

00:25.020 --> 00:31.690
nureta hitomi no oku

00:25.020 --> 00:31.690
Deep behind its wavering stare

00:33.400 --> 00:43.710
aoi tsuki wa shizuka ni koboreochiteyuku

00:33.400 --> 00:43.710
The pale moon quietly descends

00:33.480 --> 00:42.730
Yami no Matsuei

00:50.020 --> 00:55.890
azayaka na sekai wa

00:50.020 --> 00:55.890
The splendid world

00:58.260 --> 01:08.330
oto mo naku shizuka ni yami ni kieteyuku

00:58.260 --> 01:08.330
Disappears into the darkness without a sound

01:08.430 --> 01:16.070
byouyomi no naka kakemeguru yami no naka o

01:08.430 --> 01:16.070
Running about in the dark as time runs out

01:16.170 --> 01:22.700
soshite aratanaru toki o mukae ima

01:16.170 --> 01:22.700
A new era beckons now

01:25.420 --> 01:30.510
kizutsuita kuroi tsubasa

01:25.420 --> 01:30.510
The injured black wings

01:30.690 --> 01:37.060
tsuki no akari ni terasarete

01:30.690 --> 01:37.060
Shine in the moonlight

01:37.660 --> 01:41.860
utsukushiku maiagare

01:37.660 --> 01:41.860
Rising upward in a beautiful dance

01:42.000 --> 01:47.200
shinku no kuchizuke ga ima

01:42.000 --> 01:47.200
The crimson kiss

01:47.310 --> 01:54.140
kokoro no oku ni nagarekomu

01:47.310 --> 01:54.140
Flows deeply into the soul

01:54.310 --> 02:00.110
soshite yume no naka e

01:54.310 --> 02:00.110
Penetrating into one's dreams

02:08.850 --> 02:10.650
I'm not even human.

02:10.750 --> 02:12.480
I was killed by Muraki.

02:12.590 --> 02:15.610
I am one who no longer lives in this world.

02:15.720 --> 02:18.450
You're not human?

02:18.890 --> 02:20.860
I am a Shinigami.

02:20.960 --> 02:24.400
I am a Shinigami who wanted
revenge against Muraki.

02:24.830 --> 02:27.820
I don't believe that.

02:28.400 --> 02:31.370
If you doubt me, I'll prove it to you.

02:33.010 --> 02:34.440
What are you going to do?!

02:35.510 --> 02:36.700
Don't!

02:43.080 --> 02:46.320
In order to solve a particular case,

02:46.420 --> 02:49.750
I used Azumi's name to get onto this ship.

02:50.420 --> 02:53.660
I pretended to be a regular human being

02:53.760 --> 02:55.990
and spied on all of you.

02:56.100 --> 02:57.360
I'm sorry.

02:58.000 --> 03:01.200
I'm sorry for lying to you
for all this time. I'm sorry.

03:01.940 --> 03:03.200
Azumi...

03:07.940 --> 03:12.610
How could you hate someone
so much even in death?

03:13.350 --> 03:16.280
To suffer the burden of that hatred

03:16.380 --> 03:21.410
only means that you're not
able to free yourself from him.

03:21.690 --> 03:23.590
Just like me.

03:24.260 --> 03:25.490
Princess Tsubaki...

03:37.210 --> 03:42.220
Episode 9: The King of Swords, Part 3

03:54.890 --> 03:58.290
I'm all alone now.

03:58.390 --> 04:01.520
My father and the doctor
are no longer here.

04:01.630 --> 04:03.100
Why?

04:03.200 --> 04:05.690
Why do the people who are important to me

04:05.800 --> 04:07.430
disappear before me?

04:09.440 --> 04:11.170
Eileen too?

04:13.170 --> 04:15.010
- H-How do you know?
- I'm sorry.

04:15.480 --> 04:18.570
I have the ability to read other people's minds.

04:19.510 --> 04:22.680
I happened to see it yesterday
as I was tending to you.

04:23.380 --> 04:25.350
I see.

04:28.320 --> 04:31.920
Eileen was the only friend I had.

04:33.330 --> 04:36.660
While I was living in Hong Kong
because of my father's job

04:36.760 --> 04:41.460
I met Eileen, who was a
flower seller near where I lived.

04:44.740 --> 04:47.070
We just naturally became friends

04:47.170 --> 04:49.940
and when it came time
for me to return to Japan,

04:50.040 --> 04:53.100
she was hired by Father to be my playmate

04:53.210 --> 04:55.980
and she came aboard this ship with me.

05:02.060 --> 05:07.190
But she suddenly vanished.
Without saying a word to me.

05:12.530 --> 05:15.660
Azumi, can I ask you one favor?

05:15.770 --> 05:16.790
Huh?

05:16.900 --> 05:19.600
Even if it's just until we get to Hong Kong

05:19.710 --> 05:22.730
do you think you can stay close to me?

05:23.140 --> 05:24.940
I'm not Azumi.

05:25.050 --> 05:28.070
Oh, that's right.
What should I call you then?

05:28.350 --> 05:29.610
Hisoka.

05:29.880 --> 05:32.280
My name is Kurosaki Hisoka.

05:36.720 --> 05:38.320
Well, good night.

05:38.430 --> 05:40.760
Will you be all right alone?

05:40.860 --> 05:43.330
I'm not a child, you know.
You don't have to worry.

05:43.430 --> 05:45.520
If something happens, I'll shout for you.

05:45.630 --> 05:47.400
- All right.
- See you, Hisoka.

06:13.330 --> 06:16.420
You're back.
Sorry for making such a mess.

06:16.530 --> 06:18.500
What are you two doing?

06:18.600 --> 06:21.400
Wakabayashi had a microchip.

06:21.700 --> 06:24.330
Thinking there might be some clue there

06:24.440 --> 06:26.410
we were doing some analysis.

06:26.510 --> 06:29.170
- But it's pretty hard work.
- I see.

06:29.440 --> 06:31.470
Hisoka, you look kind of pale.

06:31.580 --> 06:33.170
- Get some rest.
- But...

06:33.280 --> 06:36.180
Just leave all of this to us.
All right?

06:38.050 --> 06:39.990
You're awfully kind, Tsuzuki-san.

06:40.090 --> 06:42.820
Well, he's my partner.

06:51.600 --> 06:54.730
Hello? Uh, yes, sir.

06:56.140 --> 06:59.040
Yes. The preparations have been made.

06:59.140 --> 07:00.270
I understand.

07:00.880 --> 07:02.900
<i>I will go and meet you.</i>

07:11.450 --> 07:12.710
No!

07:12.990 --> 07:14.820
Hisoka! Hisoka!

07:16.390 --> 07:18.150
You all right?

07:25.230 --> 07:27.790
<i>Why am I having those nightmares now?</i>

07:29.870 --> 07:32.200
I was able to open it!

07:32.640 --> 07:34.340
It's the data from the microchip.

07:34.440 --> 07:36.640
Good work, Gushoushin!

07:37.710 --> 07:39.540
How many files are there?!

07:39.650 --> 07:44.080
Don't complain to me.
Anyway, let's start at the top.

07:44.190 --> 07:45.210
What about here?

07:45.520 --> 07:46.650
What the heck is this?

07:46.750 --> 07:49.750
The Queen Camellia.
The blueprints for this ship?

07:49.960 --> 07:52.290
But what are these Xs?

07:53.930 --> 07:56.660
Gushoushin, get in touch
with the Judgment Bureau.

07:56.760 --> 07:57.890
Roger!

08:00.330 --> 08:03.600
Boss, we have a message from Tsuzuki-san.

08:07.010 --> 08:08.410
I see.

08:08.840 --> 08:09.940
- Tatsumi.
- Yes, sir.

08:10.040 --> 08:12.910
Get a hold of the public security
people and order a deployment.

08:13.010 --> 08:15.740
I want you to go and give Tsuzuki
and them some support.

08:15.850 --> 08:16.820
Yes, sir.

08:27.530 --> 08:28.890
<i>Princess Tsubaki.</i>

08:39.170 --> 08:41.510
- Hey, Hisoka?
- Uh, right.

08:46.380 --> 08:47.970
It's around here.

08:48.820 --> 08:51.280
It just looks like a cargo hold to me.

08:51.390 --> 08:54.250
I guess we'll just have to
start searching through it.

08:54.360 --> 08:55.410
Yeah.

08:59.830 --> 09:00.990
That's strange.

09:01.100 --> 09:03.150
There's nothing particularly unusual here.

09:03.260 --> 09:04.890
I hope this is the right place.

09:16.310 --> 09:17.800
Hey, Hisoka!

09:18.850 --> 09:19.840
What's the matter?

09:19.950 --> 09:22.180
I need you to give me a hand.

09:36.300 --> 09:38.060
What the hell is this?

09:42.900 --> 09:44.560
This is--

09:51.510 --> 09:53.100
Princess Tsubaki...

09:59.520 --> 10:00.420
Watch out!

10:00.850 --> 10:05.480
Yami no Matsuei

10:08.600 --> 10:10.220
Hisoka!

10:12.170 --> 10:13.260
What's this all about?

10:13.370 --> 10:15.730
That's what I want to ask.

10:15.840 --> 10:18.100
You've been sneaking around all over the place.

10:18.210 --> 10:19.190
Princess Tsubaki!

10:19.310 --> 10:21.500
I am not Princess Tsubaki.

10:21.610 --> 10:22.940
I am Eileen.

10:24.040 --> 10:27.210
Tsubaki's transplanted heart belongs to me!

10:27.310 --> 10:28.510
What?!

10:28.620 --> 10:29.670
What do you mean?

10:30.320 --> 10:31.680
You guys are slow.

10:31.790 --> 10:33.550
Don't you get it yet?

10:33.650 --> 10:34.620
Right here.

10:34.720 --> 10:38.180
Kakyouin has been using this
ship to do organ transplants.

10:38.290 --> 10:41.190
He takes apart people he captures in Hong Kong

10:41.300 --> 10:44.160
and illegally sells and transplants the pieces.

10:48.870 --> 10:50.500
Note: Tsubaki means Camellia Flower.

10:48.870 --> 10:50.500
<i>I'll give you this camellia.</i>

10:52.210 --> 10:56.670
Tsubaki took me, nothing
but a lowly flower seller

10:56.780 --> 10:59.680
and made me her best friend.

11:00.080 --> 11:02.210
I was willing to leave my home

11:02.320 --> 11:04.980
if it meant seeing Tsubaki's smiling face.

11:05.090 --> 11:06.950
But those men weren't like that.

11:07.550 --> 11:09.390
After all those assurances

11:09.490 --> 11:12.360
they forced themselves on me and cut me up.

11:13.130 --> 11:15.250
What kind of a betrayal is that?!

11:15.360 --> 11:17.350
I was totally taken in!

11:17.460 --> 11:20.430
So is that why you then
killed them and the owner?

11:20.530 --> 11:21.800
That's right.

11:21.900 --> 11:23.770
They all deserved to die!

11:26.970 --> 11:31.470
I killed Wakabayashi because
he was extorting Kakyouin.

11:35.950 --> 11:40.820
Muraki because he transplanted
my heart into Tsubaki.

11:44.730 --> 11:45.990
I killed Hojo...

11:46.090 --> 11:50.290
because she tried to extort Kakyouin
after Wakabayashi was dead.

11:51.670 --> 11:54.790
And then I killed Kakyouin in the end.

11:55.040 --> 11:57.200
I made him hang himself

11:57.300 --> 12:02.260
by terrifying him into thinking
he was the next to be killed.

12:02.880 --> 12:05.740
Kakyouin was easily
manipulated by that man

12:05.850 --> 12:08.540
and continued to prosper
from his trade in organs.

12:08.650 --> 12:10.010
Of course he deserved it.

12:10.120 --> 12:12.020
Who do you mean by "that man"?

12:12.690 --> 12:13.740
You fool.

12:13.850 --> 12:15.580
You still don't get it?

12:15.690 --> 12:17.250
The meaning of the King of Swords?

12:17.860 --> 12:18.980
I'll tell you.

12:19.090 --> 12:21.120
The one who was closest to Kakyouin

12:21.230 --> 12:22.990
the one who was blackmail--

12:29.100 --> 12:30.800
Princess Tsubaki!

12:33.310 --> 12:35.870
I think you've said enough, Eileen.

12:36.140 --> 12:37.270
Muraki!

12:37.380 --> 12:39.210
Were you still alive?!

12:39.310 --> 12:41.110
How naive.

12:41.220 --> 12:45.210
Did you really think I was going to die so easily?

12:45.320 --> 12:48.080
So you were behind all of this after all.

12:48.190 --> 12:51.120
Who else could there possibly be?

12:51.290 --> 12:53.850
You're awfully slow getting the picture.

12:53.960 --> 12:57.400
To think I even gave you a hint
with the King of Swords.

12:57.900 --> 13:00.370
The "counselor" in this story

13:00.470 --> 13:03.630
as well as the "cruel man"
who committed the crimes.

13:03.740 --> 13:05.760
That would be me.

13:06.040 --> 13:11.500
Kakyouin had this ship built in
order to find his daughter a heart.

13:11.850 --> 13:12.830
What?!

13:13.250 --> 13:16.580
Only a heart transplant
could save Princess Tsubaki.

13:16.680 --> 13:19.740
He said he didn't care if it was illegal

13:19.850 --> 13:22.550
so he was quite interested in my proposal.

13:23.190 --> 13:25.920
However, the heart most
suited to Princess Tsubaki

13:26.030 --> 13:27.760
belonged to Eileen.

13:27.860 --> 13:30.020
As soon as he was able to save his daughter

13:30.130 --> 13:32.260
Kakyouin wanted out of this business.

13:32.700 --> 13:35.860
He seemed to dislike illegal businesses.

13:35.970 --> 13:37.770
Unfair, don't you think?

13:37.870 --> 13:40.840
He wanted to keep all the
good fortune for himself.

13:40.940 --> 13:44.210
That's why I placed Princess
Tsubaki under hypnosis.

13:44.550 --> 13:48.610
<i>Princess Tsubaki, I'll tell you
who the donor of your heart was.</i>

13:48.720 --> 13:50.580
<i>But don't tell your father.</i>

13:50.820 --> 13:51.790
<i>Huh?</i>

13:52.590 --> 13:54.350
<i>For that heart...</i>

13:55.690 --> 13:58.520
She had to kill her friend
so she'd be able to live.

13:58.630 --> 14:00.390
I used her sense of guilt

14:00.490 --> 14:04.190
to make her think Eileen lived within her.

14:04.970 --> 14:08.560
Every time she took the medicine
to fight the rejection of the heart

14:08.670 --> 14:10.530
I cast a spell on her.

14:18.650 --> 14:19.740
Doctor...

14:20.650 --> 14:23.080
you were still alive.

14:24.350 --> 14:25.720
Princess Tsubaki.

14:26.250 --> 14:29.190
I love you, Doctor.

14:29.860 --> 14:31.350
Doctor...

14:31.930 --> 14:33.320
Doctor...

14:38.130 --> 14:40.360
But I don't love you.

14:40.470 --> 14:41.870
Why would you say that?!

14:41.970 --> 14:44.600
Princess Tsubaki has adored you all this time.

14:44.910 --> 14:47.000
Love and adoration

14:47.110 --> 14:50.470
are nothing more than
a by-product of infatuation.

14:50.580 --> 14:52.070
It's just an illusion.

14:52.180 --> 14:53.310
Why, you!

14:58.790 --> 15:01.450
Oh, right. I have planted a bomb on this ship.

15:01.560 --> 15:04.180
This ship will sink soon.

15:04.290 --> 15:06.420
I must get rid of any evidence.

15:06.690 --> 15:08.750
You think it'll go so easily?

15:08.860 --> 15:09.850
Of course.

15:09.960 --> 15:14.060
Why do you think I made it
so you can't use the wireless?

15:14.170 --> 15:15.400
- Excuse me.
- Muraki!

15:16.000 --> 15:18.440
Hisoka? The doctor...

15:18.540 --> 15:21.300
The doctor was alive, right?

15:21.410 --> 15:25.110
I wasn't just seeing things, was I?

15:27.450 --> 15:29.180
Why?

15:29.280 --> 15:33.380
Why do you still believe in him
after what he did to you?

15:33.990 --> 15:35.220
Hold it, Muraki!

15:35.460 --> 15:37.290
You're an awfully persistent man.

15:37.660 --> 15:39.020
Why are you doing this?!

15:39.730 --> 15:43.360
I never thought you people would be on this ship.

15:43.460 --> 15:47.520
But since you were, I figured I'd
make it a little more interesting.

15:47.870 --> 15:49.430
By administering poison

15:49.540 --> 15:52.530
and leaving tarot cards
and messages behind.

15:52.640 --> 15:55.510
I lent a hand to Eileen's plan.

16:00.550 --> 16:06.250
I'm sorry, Hisoka.
I made a promise to myself.

16:06.690 --> 16:08.990
That if I could fall in love with you

16:09.090 --> 16:12.220
I'd give up my love for the doctor.

16:13.090 --> 16:15.620
But I couldn't do it.

16:15.730 --> 16:17.360
But why him?

16:17.460 --> 16:21.660
He doesn't treat us like human beings.

16:21.770 --> 16:25.330
To him, we're nothing but dolls
that he can just throw away.

16:25.440 --> 16:26.910
But still you...

16:27.440 --> 16:29.600
Are you aware, Tsuzuki-san

16:29.710 --> 16:33.240
that organ transplants are on
the cutting edge of technology?

16:33.350 --> 16:38.080
There's no guarantee that the
transplant organ will be accepted.

16:38.420 --> 16:41.680
We have to overcome that
annoying thing called rejection.

16:41.790 --> 16:44.020
After all the trouble of transplanting it

16:44.120 --> 16:48.290
the organ becomes a detriment
if it isn't suited to the recipient.

16:49.200 --> 16:52.930
However, there is one method.

16:53.300 --> 16:56.700
If the organ was created from
the recipient's own cells

16:56.800 --> 16:59.000
the body won't reject it.

16:59.740 --> 17:03.140
- What are you talking about?
- You see, Tsuzuki-san...

17:03.240 --> 17:07.700
I was using this ship to do
research on those methods.

17:07.810 --> 17:11.220
That research is finally starting to bear fruit.

17:11.320 --> 17:16.150
I figured I ought to eliminate all
those who knew of my research.

17:16.260 --> 17:17.750
Research?!

17:17.860 --> 17:19.880
What do you think human lives are?!

17:19.990 --> 17:22.690
How many people did you have to kill for this?!

17:23.160 --> 17:24.860
That's so like you.

17:25.430 --> 17:28.460
You're very particular when
it comes to people dying.

17:28.570 --> 17:32.400
Your spirit is broken whenever
someone is killed in front of you.

17:32.510 --> 17:34.500
I enjoy seeing that.

17:34.610 --> 17:37.080
It's hypocritical.
It disgusts me.

17:37.180 --> 17:38.640
Muraki!

17:42.120 --> 17:43.480
You know...

17:43.580 --> 17:47.420
maybe it was because I was with him for so long.

17:48.560 --> 17:51.350
That's why I couldn't tell...

17:51.460 --> 17:55.220
whether he was a good man or a bad man.

17:55.860 --> 17:59.060
But regardless of what's happening now...

18:00.000 --> 18:03.660
I still believe in that man who
lived his life as a doctor.

18:04.940 --> 18:06.770
I recall...

18:07.140 --> 18:09.270
the day that I met you.

18:09.840 --> 18:12.780
At first I thought I could just watch you.

18:13.010 --> 18:17.710
But I began to feel like touching
that beautiful hair and body of yours.

18:18.190 --> 18:21.640
And right now, I desire you more than anything.

18:22.160 --> 18:26.680
You make my desires grow by the minute.

18:27.060 --> 18:28.550
That's what you do to me.

18:29.800 --> 18:30.760
Stop it!

18:37.740 --> 18:39.710
In the past...

18:39.810 --> 18:44.110
even he was a man who was
sincerely dedicated to saving lives.

18:44.380 --> 18:45.470
Muraki!

18:48.250 --> 18:50.310
Good-bye, Tsuzuki-san.

18:50.420 --> 18:54.080
One day I'll come around to
see you bearing a million roses.

18:54.490 --> 18:56.350
Muraki!

18:58.890 --> 19:00.260
<i>Please stay calm!</i>

19:00.360 --> 19:04.190
<i>Follow the instructions of the crew
and make your way to the lifeboats!</i>

19:04.300 --> 19:06.960
Tsuzuki-san! Hisoka-san!

19:07.730 --> 19:10.760
Hisoka, I have a favor to ask.

19:11.400 --> 19:13.270
Please kill me.

19:16.340 --> 19:17.640
Please!

19:23.050 --> 19:26.540
Tsuzuki-san! Hisoka-san!

19:27.120 --> 19:29.020
Hisoka... Hisoka!

19:35.000 --> 19:36.990
Please don't be sad, Hisoka.

19:37.800 --> 19:41.670
Although I won't be able to stay close to you...

19:41.770 --> 19:45.360
I know that you have someone
who feels strongly for you.

19:45.470 --> 19:46.440
Hisoka!

19:52.780 --> 19:54.840
Close to you...

19:55.680 --> 19:58.280
there is someone who loves you.

20:00.390 --> 20:02.550
Hisoka! Hisoka!

20:02.760 --> 20:04.720
- Tsuzuki...
- Let's go.

20:08.530 --> 20:10.330
It's going down.

20:10.430 --> 20:13.130
The ship, the money, and the cargo.

20:13.400 --> 20:15.700
But thank goodness we made it.

20:15.800 --> 20:18.270
The crew and passengers
were anesthetized with gas

20:18.370 --> 20:20.530
and the public security section has taken over.

20:20.640 --> 20:23.300
They're going to be taken to Hong Kong.

20:23.410 --> 20:25.040
After erasing their memories.

20:25.780 --> 20:27.940
Getting rid of evidence, huh?

20:28.050 --> 20:32.640
Tsuzuki...
I killed Princess Tsubaki.

20:43.130 --> 20:46.590
I shot her in the heart with Muraki's gun.

20:52.640 --> 20:57.630
Tsubaki's blood won't come off of my hands.

21:00.110 --> 21:01.380
Hisoka...

21:26.040 --> 21:27.510
How unsightly.

21:40.420 --> 21:43.420
Next Episode

21:42.520 --> 21:44.990
A deep wish.

21:45.290 --> 21:46.320
A hope.

21:47.090 --> 21:49.150
The words cannot be seen.

21:49.260 --> 21:51.420
I run towards the other.

21:52.730 --> 21:57.190
My beloved one.
Come and find me quickly.

22:00.190 --> 22:10.370
Episode 10   The Kyoto Arc, Part 1

22:00.270 --> 22:04.680
Next time on Yami no Matsuei: The Kyoto Arc, Part 1 .

22:05.450 --> 22:08.570
Those who live in the darkness wander aimlessly.

22:18.710 --> 22:22.070
arumikan no marui en o mashikaku ni orinagara

22:18.710 --> 22:22.070
As I square the round edges on the drink

22:22.180 --> 22:25.110
kimi o matsu machikado sa

22:22.180 --> 22:25.110
I wait for you on the street corner

22:25.210 --> 22:28.700
nakami no ekitai wa mou nurukute nomenai kedo

22:25.210 --> 22:28.700
The liquid inside is warm and I can't drink it anymore

22:28.820 --> 22:31.410
shikatanaku motsu ore sa

22:28.820 --> 22:31.410
But what can I do but hold onto to it?

22:31.520 --> 22:38.750
yami no naka de ore o utsusu
garasu keesu ni kazarareta

22:31.520 --> 22:38.750
In the glass case reflecting me in the darkness

22:38.860 --> 22:45.490
ningyou ga sakki kara kowai
kao de ore o miteru

22:38.860 --> 22:45.490
There is a doll that has been scowling at me

22:58.950 --> 23:05.370
ore no fuku kuchibue wa wari
to akarui uta de

22:58.950 --> 23:05.370
The tune I whistle is a bright and cheerful one

23:05.890 --> 23:11.820
zensekai no hitotachi ni
sasagerareta noizu

23:05.890 --> 23:11.820
A little noise dedicated to the people of the world

23:12.590 --> 23:18.930
dare hitori shiru hazu
no nai kono merodi ga

23:12.590 --> 23:18.930
No one could possibly recognize the melody

23:19.680 --> 23:25.080
omae ni wa kikoeru ka? Sayonara da
Love me

23:19.680 --> 23:25.080
But do you hear it?
Good-bye, Love me
